# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  FintechSaaS — Environment Variables
# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
#  HOW TO USE
#  ──────────
#  1.  Copy this file:        cp .env.example .env
#  2.  Fill in real values    (see "WHERE TO GET" notes below each section)
#  3.  NEVER commit .env      (.gitignore already covers it)
#  4.  Reload services:       npm run docker:down && npm run docker:up
#
#  QUICK START FOR REVIEWERS
#  ─────────────────────────
#  Only the variables marked ⭐ REQUIRED need to be set for the demo to work.
#  Everything else has sensible defaults and can be left commented out.
#
# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════


# ─── ⭐ REQUIRED — AI features (receipt OCR + policy insights) ──────────
#
#  Where to get: https://console.groq.com/keys (free tier — ~30 RPM)
#  Without this: OCR returns mock data (REWE GmbH 47.80 €) and policy
#                insights fall back to static text. App still runs.
#
GROQ_API_KEY=
GROQ_MODEL=llama-3.3-70b-versatile
GROQ_VISION_MODEL=meta-llama/llama-4-scout-17b-16e-instruct


# ─── ⭐ REQUIRED — Demo user credentials ────────────────────────────────
#
#  These are the four one-click-login accounts on the /auth/login screen.
#  In production you'd point AUTH0_* at your real tenant; for the portfolio
#  demo, these emails+passwords live in your local Auth0 tenant or
#  LocalStack Cognito (see localstack/ folder).
#
DEMO_EMPLOYEE_EMAIL=employee@portfolio.app
DEMO_EMPLOYEE_PASSWORD=
DEMO_MANAGER_EMAIL=manager@portfolio.app
DEMO_MANAGER_PASSWORD=
DEMO_FINANCE_EMAIL=finance@portfolio.app
DEMO_FINANCE_PASSWORD=
DEMO_ADMIN_EMAIL=admin@portfolio.app
DEMO_ADMIN_PASSWORD=
# Fresh employee — no user_profiles row, triggers onboarding flow.
DEMO_NEW_EMPLOYEE_EMAIL=new-employee@portfolio.app
DEMO_NEW_EMPLOYEE_PASSWORD=


# ─── Auth0 / Cognito ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
#  Required if NOT using LocalStack Cognito. For offline demos, leave blank
#  and the BFF will reject API calls — set up LocalStack instead (see
#  localstack/README.md).
#
#  Where to get (Auth0): Application → Settings → Domain, Client ID/Secret
#  AUDIENCE = the API identifier you registered for the Spring backend.
#
AUTH0_DOMAIN=
AUTH0_CLIENT_ID=
AUTH0_CLIENT_SECRET=
AUTH0_AUDIENCE=


# ─── Object storage (receipts) ──────────────────────────────────────────
#
#  Two options:
#
#  (a) MinIO (local, recommended for demo)
#      Uncomment the lines below and run:
#        docker compose --profile minio up -d
#      Bucket "receipts" is auto-created on first run.
#
#  B2_ENDPOINT=http://minio:9000
#  B2_APPLICATION_KEY_ID=minioadmin
#  B2_APPLICATION_KEY=minioadmin
#  B2_BUCKET_NAME=receipts
#  B2_REGION=us-east-1
#
#  (b) Backblaze B2 (production-style; free tier 10 GB)
#      Where to get: https://www.backblaze.com/b2/cloud-storage.html
#      Bucket must allow public reads OR use signed URLs (default).
#
B2_ENDPOINT=
B2_APPLICATION_KEY_ID=
B2_APPLICATION_KEY=
B2_BUCKET_NAME=receipts
B2_REGION=us-west-004


# ─── MySQL (overrides for the bundled container) ────────────────────────
#
#  Defaults are fine for local demos. Override only if you point the
#  backend at an external DB.
#
# MYSQL_ROOT_PASSWORD=12345678
# MYSQL_DATABASE=mydb


# ─── BFF / Frontend wiring ──────────────────────────────────────────────
#
#  Almost never overridden — only useful if you run services on non-default
#  hosts (e.g. behind a real reverse proxy).
#
# JAVA_API_URL=http://spring-backend:8080
# NEXT_PUBLIC_BFF_URL=/api
